<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tenmokuzan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1582</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tenmokuzan was fought in April 1582 in Kai Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, when the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> invaded the Takeda lands. Abandoned by most of his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, Takeda Katsuyori was cornered near Mount Tenmoku and killed himself with his son and remaining followers. His death ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-clan">Takeda clan</a> as a ruling house.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tenmokuzan.jpg" alt="Battle of Tenmokuzan" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utagawa Kunitsuna · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Katsuyori_died_at_Mt.Tenmoku_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
